Copyright 2026 GemmaJev contributors

The Gemma forward adapter follows the layer order of google/tunix (Apache-2.0).
Tunix copyright: Google LLC. The adapter is modified to return hidden states
for candidate scoring instead of decoding the vocabulary.

NanoJev inspired the state/question/candidate interface and comparison demo
presentation. TypeSafe Jev and NanoJev are separate projects. This repository
does not reproduce Jev's proprietary training method or claim affiliation.

The Apple GPU inference adapter uses Apple MLX and MLX-LM (MIT).
Pinned NanoJev source is downloaded separately with its MIT license preserved.
Gemma weights and downloaded datasets retain their respective terms.
